### Async Core - Testing Workflow
### Use this file with VS Code REST Client extension
### Or copy individual requests to curl commands

### ============================================
### SECTION 1: Health Checks
### ============================================

### Check Server Health
GET http://localhost:3000/health
Content-Type: application/json

### Check Queue Health
GET http://localhost:3000/api/queue/health
Content-Type: application/json

### ============================================
### SECTION 2: Submit Email Jobs
### ============================================

### Submit Bulk Emails (2 recipients)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipients": ["alice@example.com", "bob@example.com"],
  "subject": "Welcome to Async Core",
  "message": "This is a test email from the background processing system"
}

### Submit Single Email
POST http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipients": ["test@example.com"],
  "subject": "Single Test Email",
  "message": "Testing single email submission"
}

### Submit Many Emails (10 recipients)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipients": [
    "user1@example.com",
    "user2@example.com",
    "user3@example.com",
    "user4@example.com",
    "user5@example.com",
    "user6@example.com",
    "user7@example.com",
    "user8@example.com",
    "user9@example.com",
    "user10@example.com"
  ],
  "subject": "Bulk Email Test",
  "message": "Testing bulk email submission with 10 recipients"
}

### ============================================
### SECTION 3: Email Queue Statistics
### ============================================

### Get Email Queue Stats (Main Queue)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/stats
Content-Type: application/json

### Get Queue Health Check
GET http://localhost:3000/api/queue/stats
Content-Type: application/json

### ============================================
### SECTION 4: Job Status Tracking
### ============================================
### Note: Replace JOB_ID with actual job ID from submission response

### Get Job Status - Example (replace JOB_ID)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs/email-1234567890-abc123
Content-Type: application/json

### ============================================
### SECTION 5: Error Testing
### ============================================

### Missing Recipients (should fail with 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "No Recipients",
  "message": "This should fail"
}

### Empty Recipients Array (should fail with 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipients": [],
  "subject": "Empty Recipients",
  "message": "This should fail"
}

### Missing Subject (should fail with 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipients": ["test@example.com"],
  "message": "No subject"
}

### Missing Message (should fail with 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "recipients": ["test@example.com"],
  "subject": "No Message"
}

### Invalid Job ID (should fail with 404)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/jobs/email/jobs/invalid-job-id-12345
Content-Type: application/json
